{=============================================================================
  Crossflow tube banks: Nusselt-number correlations and row / angle
  correction factors
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0095 (function library, kind = function)
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Six correlations and correction factors of the forced convection across a bank
  of plain tubes: the Nusselt number of the bundle (Zukauskas with the Bejan
  fit, ESDU 73031 as given by Hewitt, the Heat Exchanger Design Handbook) and
  the tube-row correction factor of Zukauskas and of ESDU 73031 with its
  tube-bank inclination correction factor.

  Every function returns the Nusselt number with respect to the tube OUTSIDE
  diameter; the heat-transfer coefficient follows from h = Nu*k/Do and is left
  to the caller. All arguments are dimensionless except the tube outside
  diameter Do [m] and the two pitches [m]; Re, Pr, Pr_wall and the number of
  tube rows are inputs (no property function is called inside the functions).

  Two Python arguments that are optional in ht are mandatory here, because EES
  has no optional arguments: Pr_wall (Zukauskas, ESDU) - pass Pr_wall = Pr for
  the uncorrected form - and the flags staggered (Zukauskas, ESDU row factor)
  and, for the inclination angle, the angle itself in degrees.

  The seventh function of the ht family, Nu_Grimison_tube_bank, is NOT
  translated: in ht the two tabulated Grimison coefficients C1 and m are read
  from a bivariate least-squares spline surface fitted to the digitised tables
  (ht/conv_tube_bank.py, bisplev on pre-generated splines of degree (3,3) inline
  and (1,1) staggered); it is not a closed-form correlation, and a linear
  interpolation of the published tables is a different function. See README.md.

  The demonstration program at the end calls every function, once with the
  inputs of the ht doctest of the corresponding correlation ("A" cases) and
  once with a second, uniform input set ("B" cases). The ht values of both sets
  are tabulated in the README (verification table).

  Inputs : Re [-], Pr [-], Pr_wall [-], tube_rows [-], staggered flag [-],
           pitch_parallel [m], pitch_normal [m], Do [m], angle [deg]
  Outputs: Nu [-], F [-] (one FUNCTION per correlation / correction factor)
  Units  : SI - dimensionless numbers, lengths in m, angles in degrees
  Source : ht (Caleb Bell), ht/conv_tube_bank.py, version 1.2.0, commit 85e0ee6,
           MIT - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht ; correlations by the authors
           cited in each function block - see README.md
  Status : VERIFIED against the doctests and the values of ht 1.2.0
           (README.md, "Verification")
=============================================================================}

FUNCTION Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(tube_rows, staggered, Re)
{ZUKAUSKAS_TUBE_ROW_CORRECTION - tube row count correction factor for crossflow
across a tube bundle, read from a graph digitised from [1]. The factors are
slightly different for the staggered and for the in-line configuration; for the
staggered configuration, factors are given separately for Re below and above
1000. The basis of the method is that an infinitely long tube bank has a factor
of 1, in practice reached at 20 rows (as in ht).

  F = F(n)   n = tube rows, F = 1 for n >= 20, F(1) for n < 1

  n    staggered, Re < 1000    staggered, Re >= 1000    in-line
  1         0.8295                 0.6273              0.6768
  2         0.8792                 0.7689              0.8089
  3         0.9151                 0.8473              0.8687
  4         0.9402                 0.8942              0.9054
  5         0.9570                 0.9254              0.9303
  6         0.9677                 0.9450              0.9465
  7         0.9745                 0.9570              0.9569
  8         0.9785                 0.9652              0.9647
  9         0.9808                 0.9716              0.9712
  10        0.9823                 0.9765              0.9766
  11        0.9838                 0.9803              0.9811
  12        0.9855                 0.9834              0.9847
  13        0.9873                 0.9862              0.9877
  14        0.9891                 0.9890              0.9900
  15        0.9910                 0.9918              0.9920
  16        0.9929                 0.9943              0.9937
  17        0.9948                 0.9965              0.9953
  18        0.9967                 0.9980              0.9969
  19        0.9987                 0.9986              0.9986

tube_rows [-] is the number of tube rows per bundle, staggered = 1 for a
staggered and 0 for an in-line bank, Re [-] is the Reynolds number of the flow
through the bundle on the bare tube outside diameter and the minimum flow area.
Validity: as in ht, no limits quoted.
Original: Zukauskas, A. Heat transfer from tubes in crossflow. In T.F. Irvine,
  Jr. and J. P. Hartnett, editors, Advances in Heat Transfer, volume 8,
  pages 93-160. Academic Press, Inc., New York, 1972.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py,
  Zukauskas_tube_row_correction, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  IF tube_rows < 1 THEN
    n = 1
  ELSE
    n = tube_rows
  ENDIF
  F = 1
  IF staggered = 1 THEN
    IF Re < 1000 THEN
      F = 0.8295
      IF n = 2 THEN F = 0.8792
      IF n = 3 THEN F = 0.9151
      IF n = 4 THEN F = 0.9402
      IF n = 5 THEN F = 0.957
      IF n = 6 THEN F = 0.9677
      IF n = 7 THEN F = 0.9745
      IF n = 8 THEN F = 0.9785
      IF n = 9 THEN F = 0.9808
      IF n = 10 THEN F = 0.9823
      IF n = 11 THEN F = 0.9838
      IF n = 12 THEN F = 0.9855
      IF n = 13 THEN F = 0.9873
      IF n = 14 THEN F = 0.9891
      IF n = 15 THEN F = 0.991
      IF n = 16 THEN F = 0.9929
      IF n = 17 THEN F = 0.9948
      IF n = 18 THEN F = 0.9967
      IF n = 19 THEN F = 0.9987
    ELSE
      F = 0.6273
      IF n = 2 THEN F = 0.7689
      IF n = 3 THEN F = 0.8473
      IF n = 4 THEN F = 0.8942
      IF n = 5 THEN F = 0.9254
      IF n = 6 THEN F = 0.945
      IF n = 7 THEN F = 0.957
      IF n = 8 THEN F = 0.9652
      IF n = 9 THEN F = 0.9716
      IF n = 10 THEN F = 0.9765
      IF n = 11 THEN F = 0.9803
      IF n = 12 THEN F = 0.9834
      IF n = 13 THEN F = 0.9862
      IF n = 14 THEN F = 0.989
      IF n = 15 THEN F = 0.9918
      IF n = 16 THEN F = 0.9943
      IF n = 17 THEN F = .9965
      IF n = 18 THEN F = .998
      IF n = 19 THEN F = .9986
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    F = 0.6768
    IF n = 2 THEN F = 0.8089
    IF n = 3 THEN F = 0.8687
    IF n = 4 THEN F = 0.9054
    IF n = 5 THEN F = 0.9303
    IF n = 6 THEN F = 0.9465
    IF n = 7 THEN F = 0.9569
    IF n = 8 THEN F = 0.9647
    IF n = 9 THEN F = 0.9712
    IF n = 10 THEN F = 0.9766
    IF n = 11 THEN F = 0.9811
    IF n = 12 THEN F = 0.9847
    IF n = 13 THEN F = 0.9877
    IF n = 14 THEN F = 0.99
    IF n = 15 THEN F = 0.992
    IF n = 16 THEN F = 0.9937
    IF n = 17 THEN F = 0.9953
    IF n = 18 THEN F = 0.9969
    IF n = 19 THEN F = 0.9986
  ENDIF
  Zukauskas_tube_row_correction = F
END

FUNCTION Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan(Re, Pr, tube_rows, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, Pr_wall)
{NU_ZUKAUSKAS_BEJAN - Nusselt number for crossflow across a tube bank of tube
number n at a specified Re, according to the method of Zukauskas [1]; a fit to
graphs of [1] published by Bejan [2] is used for the correlation, the tube row
correction factor is read from digitised graphs of [1] (see
Zukauskas_tube_row_correction).

  Aligned tube banks:   Nu = C*Re^m*Pr^0.36*(Pr/Pr_wall)^0.25*Cn
    C = 0.9   m = 0.4    for Re < 100
    C = 0.52  m = 0.05   for 100 <= Re < 1000
    C = 0.27  m = 0.63   for 1000 <= Re < 2E5
    C = 0.033 m = 0.8    for Re >= 2E5

  Staggered tube banks: Nu = C*Re^m*Pr^0.36*(Pr/Pr_wall)^0.25*(Xt/Xl)^0.2*Cn
    C = 1.04  m = 0.4    (Xt/Xl)^0.2 omitted, for Re < 500
    C = 0.71  m = 0.5    (Xt/Xl)^0.2 omitted, for 500 <= Re < 1000
    C = 0.35  m = 0.6    for 1000 <= Re < 2E5
    C = 0.031 m = 0.8    for Re >= 2E5

  Xt = pitch_normal [m], Xl = pitch_parallel [m], Cn = tube row correction

Re [-] is on the tube outside diameter and the average (bulk) fluid properties,
Pr [-] and Pr_wall [-] are the Prandtl numbers at the average and at the wall
temperature; passing Pr_wall = Pr gives the form without the Prandtl number
correction (an exponent of 0.25 is recommended in [1] for heating and cooling,
for both liquids and gases). The configuration is staggered when
|pitch_normal/pitch_parallel - 1| > 0.05, as in ht.
Validity: 1 < Re < 200000 (as in ht, the four regimes above).
Original: Zukauskas, A. Heat transfer from tubes in crossflow. In T.F. Irvine,
  Jr. and J. P. Hartnett, editors, Advances in Heat Transfer, volume 8,
  pages 93-160. Academic Press, Inc., New York, 1972; presented by Bejan, A.,
  Convection Heat Transfer, 4E, Hoboken, New Jersey: Wiley, 2013.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py, Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  staggered = IF(ABS(1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel) > 0.05, 1, 0)
  f_pitch = 1
  IF staggered = 1 THEN
    IF Re < 500 THEN
      C = 1.04
      m = 0.4
    ELSE
      IF Re < 1000 THEN
        C = 0.71
        m = 0.5
      ELSE
        f_pitch = (pitch_normal/pitch_parallel)^0.2
        IF Re < 2E5 THEN
          C = 0.35
          m = 0.6
        ELSE
          C = 0.031
          m = 0.8
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    IF Re < 100 THEN
      C = 0.9
      m = 0.4
    ELSE
      IF Re < 1000 THEN
        C = 0.52
        m = 0.05
      ELSE
        IF Re < 2E5 THEN
          C = 0.27
          m = 0.63
        ELSE
          C = 0.033
          m = 0.8
        ENDIF
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  Nu = C*Re^m*Pr^0.36*f_pitch*(Pr/Pr_wall)^0.25
  Cn = Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(tube_rows, staggered, Re)
  Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan = Nu*Cn
END

FUNCTION ESDU_tube_row_correction(tube_rows, staggered)
{ESDU_TUBE_ROW_CORRECTION - tube row count correction factor for heat transfer
across a tube bundle according to [1], as shown in [2]; also used for finned
bundles. The factors are slightly different for the staggered and the in-line
configuration. Tabular lookup, with a value of 1 for 10 tube rows or more.

  F2 = F2(n)   n = tube rows; F2(3) for n <= 2, 1 for n >= 10, F2(n) for 3..9

  n     staggered    in-line
  2, 3    0.8593      0.8479
  4       0.8984      0.8957
  5       0.9268      0.9306
  6       0.9482      0.9551
  7       0.9650      0.9724
  8       0.9777      0.9839
  9       0.9868      0.9902

tube_rows [-] is the number of tube rows per bundle, staggered = 1 for a
staggered and 0 for an in-line bank. Passing tube_rows = 10 disables the
correction.
Validity: as in ht, no limits quoted. For tube counts 1-7, [3] claims the
  factors of [1] are on average 0.65, 0.77, 0.84, 0.9, 0.94, 0.97, 0.99.
Original: "Convective Heat Transfer During Crossflow of Fluids Over Plain Tube
  Banks." ESDU 73031 (November 1, 1973); as shown in Hewitt, G. L. Shires, T.
  Reg Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R. Bott, Process Heat Transfer. 1st
  edition. Boca Raton: CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py,
  ESDU_tube_row_correction, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  F2 = 1
  IF tube_rows <= 2 THEN
    IF staggered = 1 THEN
      F2 = 0.8593
    ELSE
      F2 = 0.8479
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    IF tube_rows < 10 THEN
      IF staggered = 1 THEN
        F2 = 0.8593
        IF tube_rows = 4 THEN F2 = 0.8984
        IF tube_rows = 5 THEN F2 = 0.9268
        IF tube_rows = 6 THEN F2 = 0.9482
        IF tube_rows = 7 THEN F2 = 0.965
        IF tube_rows = 8 THEN F2 = 0.9777
        IF tube_rows = 9 THEN F2 = 0.9868
      ELSE
        F2 = 0.8479
        IF tube_rows = 4 THEN F2 = 0.8957
        IF tube_rows = 5 THEN F2 = 0.9306
        IF tube_rows = 6 THEN F2 = 0.9551
        IF tube_rows = 7 THEN F2 = 0.9724
        IF tube_rows = 8 THEN F2 = 0.9839
        IF tube_rows = 9 THEN F2 = 0.9902
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  ESDU_tube_row_correction = F2
END

FUNCTION ESDU_tube_angle_correction(angle)
{ESDU_TUBE_ANGLE_CORRECTION - tube bank inclination correction factor for heat
transfer across a tube bundle according to [1].

  F3 = Nu_theta/Nu_theta=90deg = (SIN(theta))^0.6

angle [deg] is the angle of inclination of the tube bank with respect to the
longitudinal axis (90 deg for a straight tube bank); SIN takes its argument in
degrees, as everywhere in CoolSolve and EES.
Validity: 1E2 < Re < 1E6 (as in ht). For angles below 10 deg the problem should
  be considered internal flow, not flow across a tube bank (as in ht).
Original: "Convective Heat Transfer During Crossflow of Fluids Over Plain Tube
  Banks." ESDU 73031 (November 1, 1973).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py,
  ESDU_tube_angle_correction, MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  ESDU_tube_angle_correction = SIN(angle)^0.6
END

FUNCTION Nu_ESDU_73031(Re, Pr, tube_rows, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal, Pr_wall, angle)
{NU_ESDU_73031 - Nusselt number for crossflow across a tube bank with a
specified number of tube rows, at a specified Re according to [1], also shown
in [2].

  Nu = a*Re^m*Pr^0.34*F1*F2*F3

  In-line tube banks:      Staggered tube banks:
  Re       a      m        Re       a      m
  10-300   0.742  0.431    10-300   1.309  0.360
  300-2E5  0.211  0.651    300-2E5  0.273  0.635
  2E5-2E6  0.116  0.700    2E5-2E6  0.124  0.700

  F1 = (Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26   property correction factor (1 if Pr_wall = Pr)
  F2 = ESDU_tube_row_correction(tube_rows, staggered)
  F3 = ESDU_tube_angle_correction(angle)

Re [-] is on the tube outside diameter and the average (bulk) fluid properties,
Pr [-] and Pr_wall [-] are the bulk and wall Prandtl numbers; pitch_normal [m]
and pitch_parallel [m] are the transverse and the longitudinal pitch (the
configuration is staggered when |pitch_normal/pitch_parallel - 1| > 0.05, as
in ht), tube_rows [-] is the number of tube rows (10 disables F2) and angle
[deg] the inclination of the bank (90 deg for a straight bank).
Validity: in-line coefficients for a transverse pitch to tube diameter ratio of
  1.2 to 4, staggered ones from 1 to 4; the overall accuracy of the method is
  claimed to be 15%; Re from 10 to 2E6 (as in ht). A Prandtl number exponent of
  0.26 is recommended in [1] for heating and cooling, for both liquids and gases.
Original: "High-Fin Staggered Tube Banks: Heat Transfer and Pressure Drop for
  Turbulent Single Phase Gas Flow." ESDU 86022 (October 1, 1986); the same
  expressions for plain tube banks are given in ESDU 73031 (November 1, 1973);
  as shown in Hewitt, G. L. Shires, T. Reg Bott G. F., G. L. Shires and T. R.
  Bott, Process Heat Transfer. 1st edition. Boca Raton: CRC Press, 1994.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py, Nu_ESDU_73031,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  staggered = IF(ABS(1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel) > 0.05, 1, 0)
  IF staggered = 1 THEN
    IF Re <= 300 THEN
      a = 1.309
      m = 0.36
    ELSE
      IF Re <= 2E5 THEN
        a = 0.273
        m = 0.635
      ELSE
        a = 0.124
        m = 0.7
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ELSE
    IF Re <= 300 THEN
      a = 0.742
      m = 0.431
    ELSE
      IF Re <= 2E5 THEN
        a = 0.211
        m = 0.651
      ELSE
        a = 0.116
        m = 0.7
      ENDIF
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
  F1 = (Pr/Pr_wall)^0.26
  F2 = ESDU_tube_row_correction(tube_rows, staggered)
  F3 = ESDU_tube_angle_correction(angle)
  Nu_ESDU_73031 = a*Re^m*Pr^0.34*F1*F2*F3
END

FUNCTION Nu_HEDH_tube_bank(Re, Pr, Do, tube_rows, pitch_parallel, pitch_normal)
{NU_HEDH_TUBE_BANK - Nusselt number for crossflow across a tube bank of tube
rows at a specified Re, Pr and D, using the Heat Exchanger Design Handbook
(HEDH) methodology presented in [1].

  Nu = Nu_m*f_N

  Nu_m     = 0.3 + SQRT(Nu_m,lam^2 + Nu_m,turb^2)
  Nu_m,turb= 0.037*Re^0.8*Pr / {1 + 2.443*Re^(-0.1)*(Pr^(2/3) - 1)}
  Nu_m,lam = 0.664*Re^0.5*Pr^(1/3)
  psi     = 1 - pi/(4a)      if b >= 1
  psi     = 1 - pi/(4ab)     if b < 1
  f_A     = 1 + 0.7/psi^1.5*(b/a - 0.3)/(b/a + 0.7)^2   in-line
  f_A     = 1 + 2/(3b)                                   staggered
  f_N     = {1 + (n-1)*f_A}/n                           n < 10 rows
  f_N     = f_A                                          n >= 10 rows

  a = pitch_normal/Do, b = pitch_parallel/Do, Re on the corrected value
  Re of the equation above is Re/psi (Re here is the Reynolds number on the
  bare tube outside diameter and the minimum flow area through the bundle)

Do [m] is the tube outside diameter, pitch_parallel [m] the longitudinal pitch
and pitch_normal [m] the transverse pitch; the configuration is staggered when
|pitch_normal/pitch_parallel - 1| > 0.05, as in ht. A further partly staggered
tube bank correlation exists in ht, using another pitch; it is not implemented
there either.
Validity: 10 < Re < 1E5 and 0.6 < Pr < 1000 (as in ht). The Prandtl number
  correction is left to an outside function, because the coefficients given in
  [1] depend on whether heating or cooling happens and use a temperature ratio
  instead of a Prandtl number for gases.
Original: Schlunder, Ernst U, and International Center for Heat and Mass
  Transfer. Heat Exchanger Design Handbook. Washington: Hemisphere Pub. Corp.,
  1987. Example 3.11 (Re = 10263.37, Pr = 0.708, 11 rows, both pitches 0.05 m,
  Do = 0.025 m) is from Baehr, H. D. and K. Stephan, Heat and Mass Transfer,
  Springer, 2013.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/conv_tube_bank.py, Nu_HEDH_tube_bank,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  staggered = IF(ABS(1 - pitch_normal/pitch_parallel) > 0.05, 1, 0)
  a = pitch_normal/Do
  b = pitch_parallel/Do
  IF b >= 1 THEN
    psi = 1 - pi()/4/a
  ELSE
    psi = 1 - pi()/4/a/b
  ENDIF
  Re_psi = Re/psi
  Nu_laminar = 0.664*Re_psi^0.5*Pr^(1/3)
  Nu_turbulent = 0.037*Re_psi^0.8*Pr/(1 + 2.443*Re_psi^(-0.1)*(Pr^(2/3) - 1))
  Nu_m = 0.3 + (Nu_laminar^2 + Nu_turbulent^2)^0.5
  IF staggered = 1 THEN
    f_A = 1 + 2/3/b
  ELSE
    f_A = 1 + 0.7/psi^1.5*(b/a - 0.3)/(b/a + 0.7)^2
  ENDIF
  IF tube_rows < 10 THEN
    f_N = (1 + (tube_rows - 1)*f_A)/tube_rows
  ELSE
    f_N = f_A
  ENDIF
  Nu_HEDH_tube_bank = Nu_m*f_N
END

"!============================================================================="
"!Demonstration program: every correlation is called twice"
"It is ignored by the future $INCLUDE library:tube_bank_nusselt (CS-FEAT-IMPORT)."
"Case A: the input set of the ht doctest of each correlation (published values)."
"Case B: one second, uniform input set (shell side of an air-cooled bundle:"
"Re = 1.2E4, Pr = 0.71, Pr_wall = 0.8, Do = 0.025 m, 8 rows, ST = 0.07 m,"
"SL = 0.05 m, bank inclined at 60 degrees)."
"Both cases are tabulated against ht in the README (verification table)."

"Case B - input set"
Re_B = 1.2E4
Pr_B = 0.71
Pr_wall_B = 0.8
Do_B = 0.025
tube_rows_B = 8
pitch_normal_B = 0.07
pitch_parallel_B = 0.05
angle_B = 60

"Zukauskas tube row correction - 4 staggered rows, then 6 in-line rows"
Zukauskas_row_A = Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(4, 1, 1E4)
Zukauskas_row_inline_A = Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(6, 0, 1E4)
Zukauskas_row_B = Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(tube_rows_B, 1, Re_B)
Zukauskas_row_inline_B = Zukauskas_tube_row_correction(tube_rows_B, 0, Re_B)

"Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan - without and with the Prandtl number correction"
Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan_A = Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan(1E4, 7, 10, 0.05, 0.05, 7)
Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan_Prwall_A = Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan(1E4, 7, 10, 0.05, 0.05, 5)
Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan_B = Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan(Re_B, Pr_B, tube_rows_B, pitch_parallel_B, pitch_normal_B, Pr_B)
Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan_Prwall_B = Nu_Zukauskas_Bejan(Re_B, Pr_B, tube_rows_B, pitch_parallel_B, pitch_normal_B, Pr_wall_B)

"ESDU tube row correction - 4 staggered rows, then 6 in-line rows"
ESDU_row_A = ESDU_tube_row_correction(4, 1)
ESDU_row_inline_A = ESDU_tube_row_correction(6, 0)
ESDU_row_B = ESDU_tube_row_correction(tube_rows_B, 1)
ESDU_row_inline_B = ESDU_tube_row_correction(tube_rows_B, 0)

"ESDU tube inclination correction factor"
ESDU_angle_A = ESDU_tube_angle_correction(75)
ESDU_angle_B = ESDU_tube_angle_correction(angle_B)

"Nu_ESDU_73031 - its doctest, then the uniform input set"
"Nu_ESDU_73031 - uniform input set with the wall Prandtl number and the angle"
Nu_ESDU_A = Nu_ESDU_73031(1.32E4, 0.71, 8, 0.09, 0.05, 0.71, 90)
Nu_ESDU_B = Nu_ESDU_73031(Re_B, Pr_B, tube_rows_B, pitch_parallel_B, pitch_normal_B, Pr_B, 90)
Nu_ESDU_Prwall_angle_B = Nu_ESDU_73031(Re_B, Pr_B, tube_rows_B, pitch_parallel_B, pitch_normal_B, Pr_wall_B, angle_B)

"Nu_HEDH_tube_bank - its doctest, the example 3.11 of Baehr and Stephan, then"
"the uniform input set"
Nu_HEDH_A = Nu_HEDH_tube_bank(1E4, 7, 0.03, 10, 0.05, 0.05)
Nu_HEDH_ex311_A = Nu_HEDH_tube_bank(10263.37, 0.708, 0.025, 11, 0.05, 0.05)
Nu_HEDH_B = Nu_HEDH_tube_bank(Re_B, Pr_B, Do_B, tube_rows_B, pitch_parallel_B, pitch_normal_B)